      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Our programmers recommend..."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://d3cyv0xf0ss37v.cloudfront.net/2026/films/560x315/marie-madeleine-01.jpeg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "BFI London Film Festival 2026"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Marie Madeleine"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The second feature from Haitian actor-director Gessica Généus (Freda, LFF 2021) follows an unlikely friendship between a sex worker and preacher’s son that rocks their community."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://d3cyv0xf0ss37v.cloudfront.net/2026/films/560x315/9-temples-to-heaven-01.jpeg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "BFI London Film Festival 2026"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "9 Temples to Heaven"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Infused with gentle humour and profound humanity, Sompot Chidgasornpongse’s fiction debut presents a serene passage through family, faith and the cycles of life."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://d3cyv0xf0ss37v.cloudfront.net/2026/films/560x315/bas-book-01.jpeg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "BFI London Film Festival 2026"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Ba’s Book"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Ashley Duong crafts a heartfelt hybrid film in response to her father’s memoir, which recounts his experiences of the Vietnam War and Iranian Revolution."
    }
